absl is the one v8_gypfiles target that survives --without-bundled-v8, since
node.cc uses absl::Mutex, and it wants neither of the two architecture answers
the rest of this build needs. -U__i386__ (the lever v8config.h's host block
forces on everything that includes it) keeps absl off the x86 rdtsc path in
unscaledcycleclock.cc, which does not compile here. -U__linux__ is what node's
bundled libuv needs gyp's own source selection to agree with, and it also
keeps low_level_alloc.cc off the `#ifdef __linux__` include of direct_mmap.h.
Both land in cflags_cc: gyp's ninja rule spells the compile line
$cflags $cflags_cc, and the environment's CXXFLAGS are prepended to the second,
so only there does a target-specific flag come last for a C++ source. absl's C
sources take the same two undefines through cflags_c, which is the only list a
C source reads at all.

What -U__linux__ would otherwise take with it -- ABSL_HAVE_MMAP, and the four
synchronization sources whose bodies hang off it -- is restored by
abseil-config-wasm-has-mmap.patch; see that file.

Two source families are dropped outright: str_format and everything that
pulls it -- the cord families, absl/crc, container/internal/raw_hash_set.cc --
need std::wstring, which this libc++ does not provide: `no type named
'wstring' in namespace 'std'`.

--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
@@ -18,6 +18,17 @@
       },
       'include_dirs': [
         '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)',
+      ],
+      'cflags_c': [ '-U__i386__', '-U__linux__' ],
+      'cflags_cc': [ '-U__i386__', '-U__linux__' ],
+      'sources!': [
+        '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)/absl/container/internal/raw_hash_set.cc',
+      ],
+      'sources/': [
+        ['exclude', '/absl/crc/'],
+        ['exclude', '/absl/strings/cord'],
+        ['exclude', '/absl/strings/internal/cord'],
+        ['exclude', '/absl/strings/internal/str_format/'],
       ],
       'sources': [
         '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)/absl/algorithm/algorithm.h',
